# L §5.18 example ask q2, copied, over a minimal reality: "flows(x, span) is the sum of the movements into place x in
# the span, minus those out of x" (L §5.14.3): in March 2026 konto gets 2 000.00 PLN and pays 500.00 PLN: 1 500.00
# PLN.  `check e == f` prints ok, or "differs: e = …, f = …" and the difference e − f (L §5.18).  A span from before
# S makes flows a hole (HOLE-PRERUN, "before the run's start", L §8.1).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

kind accounts_pl: place PLN signed
input rec_total[x in accounts_pl, m in months]: money PLN
input pay_amt: money PLN
input rent_amt: money PLN
input pay_day: date
input rent_day: date
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..

move pay: transfers
  on pay_day
  leg cash from world to konto amount pay_amt

move rent: transfers
  on rent_day
  leg cash from konto to world amount rent_amt

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  accounts_pl + [konto] lives 2026-01-01..
  pay_amt = 2 000.00 PLN
  rent_amt = 500.00 PLN
  pay_day = 2026-03-10
  rent_day = 2026-03-05

version recs
  cite s
  governs 2026
  known 2026-04-02
  rec_total[konto, 2026-03] = 1 500.00 PLN
  rec_total[konto, 2026-04] = 100.00 PLN

ask q2: check flows(konto, 2026-03) == rec_total[konto, 2026-03] law 2026-03-31
ask q2b: check flows(konto, 2026-04) == rec_total[konto, 2026-04] law 2026-04-30
ask pre: flows(konto, 2025-12-01 .. 2026-03-31)
=== expect
pre: ?"before the run's start" (konto)
  cut 2026-12-31
q2: ok
  unfulfilled: pay
  unfulfilled: rent
  law date 2026-03-31, cut 2026-12-31
q2b: differs: flows(konto, 2026-04) = 0.00 PLN, rec_total[konto, 2026-04] = 100.00 PLN, difference -100.00 PLN
  law date 2026-04-30, cut 2026-12-31
